  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Children Online Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Safe Children Online project is a transformative initiative focused on making children and 
youth safe when being online and having easy access to support when needed. The project will 
be implemented in Chibombo district, a rural area outside Lusaka, Zambia, by the 
Lifeline/Childline project team. The project addresses critical challenges for children and youth, 
such as low awareness of OCSEA and other online risks, lack of effective reporting mechanisms, 
stigma surrounding reporting of online abuse, and insufficient resources to respond to online 
harm in rural areas. By tackling the root causes, including limited knowledge of online risks, 
inadequate protection resources, and the cultural stigma that discourages reporting, the 
initiative aspires to create a safer and more informed digital landscape for children in Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
